# RDP Logon Detection Queries

## 1. Primary RDP Detection

```spl
index=main EventCode=4624
| search Logon_Type=10
| table _time ComputerName Account_Domain Account_Name Logon_Type Logon_Process Authentication_Package IpAddress Workstation_Name
| sort - _time
```

## 2. RDP Detection With Full Event Information

```spl
index=main EventCode=4624
| search Logon_Type=10
| table _time ComputerName Account_Domain Account_Name Logon_Type Logon_Process Authentication_Package IpAddress Workstation_Name Logon_ID Message
| sort - _time
```

## 3. Count RDP Logons

```spl
index=main EventCode=4624
| search Logon_Type=10
| stats count by Account_Name IpAddress ComputerName
| sort - count
```

## 4. Investigate All Successful Logon Types

Use this query to determine which logon types are being ingested:

```spl
index=main EventCode=4624
| stats count by Logon_Type
| sort - count
```

## 5. Search for RDP Events Using Raw Event Text

If the extracted `Logon_Type` field is unavailable:

```spl
index=main EventCode=4624
| search "Logon Type: 10"
| table _time ComputerName Account_Name Message
| sort - _time
```

## Expected Detection

The primary query should return an event similar to:

```text
EventCode: 4624
Logon_Type: 10
ComputerName: TargetMachine
Account_Name: a4803
```

Logon Type 10 corresponds to RemoteInteractive/RDP logons.
